<title>USA: Wesley sells U.S. Natural Touch rights.</title>
<headline>Wesley sells U.S. Natural Touch rights.</headline>
<dateline>DES PLAINES, Ill. 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wesley Jessen VisionCare Inc said Tuesday it sold the rights to market its Natural Touch line of opaque soft contact lenses in the United States to Cooper Cos Inc in compliance with an agreement reached with the U.S. Federal Trade Commission.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Wesley Jessen manufactures and markets Natural Touch lenses in all of its international markets.</p>
<p>Wesley Jessen's pro forma revenues in 1996 were about $250 million. Natural Touch' U.S. sales were about $6.9 million for the year ending March 31, 1996.</p>
<p>	  ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
